First of all, thank you for the development of this package and the publication of insightful articles about accelerometer data processing.

For a study we're working on, I'd love to calculate the arm angle (as described in the PLOS one article by van Hees et al in 2015 (PDF <http://journals.plos.org/plosone/article/file?id=10.1371/journal.pone.0142533&type=printable>)) together with the output of g.getmeta. If I study the source code of g.getmeta, the variable Gx, Gy, Gz refer to the raw accelerometer data but are later on deleted.
Is it possible to derive the arm angle from the variables produced by g.getmeta? If not, my solution would be to add this calculation to g.applymetrics using Gx, Gy and Gz and then implement this metric in g.getmeta.

Any feedback or thoughts on this subject would be really appreciated.

